## 5. Validation and contracts

### 5.1 Validation scale

ADR 0033 D13 (accepted) is the only binding rule: **V3 requires a differential scenario against Pekko whenever an applicable oracle exists; rows that can only be validated in Go carry documented alternative evidence and explicit Owner approval; until approved they are `pending approval`; they are never marked V3 by default and never lowered silently.**

The V0 to V3 labels are this plan's working scale (the dossier's 7.2 defined them differently). The dossier's definition made V2 an unconditional "differential judge scenario", which V3 then inherited, so a Go-only row could never reach V3 without contradicting D13. This plan restates them so that the oracle condition lives only in V3:

| Level | Definition (restated) |
|---|---|
| V0 | Public-API Go test asserting every observable effect |
| V1 | V0 plus a ported or adapted upstream spec cited by name and line, with PORT-GAPs listed |
| V2 | V1 plus a Go-side scenario with a detecting mutation (no Pekko run required) |
| V3 | V2 plus `-race` and the module-close mutation campaign, **and** either (a) a passing differential scenario on Pekko and Go, when an applicable oracle exists, or (b) documented alternative evidence with explicit Owner approval, when none exists; (b) without approval is recorded as `pending approval`, not V3 |

**Revision 5 (2026-11-07): O-1 is resolved.** The Owner approved the scale on [#1467](https://github.com/getsyntegrity/gopekko/issues/1467) and it is recorded in the amendment "the V scale and what V2 and V3 require per row" of [ADR 0033](adr/0033-actor-typed-scope-and-architecture.md): the scale is cumulative (V2 requires V1, V1 requires V0, V3 requires V2): V0 and V1 are unchanged, V2 adds the coverage of every Pekko contract of the row, and V3 is superseded by the amendment (a passing differential scenario on Pekko with CURRENT evidence). The next paragraph is kept as the text of revisions 3 and 4.

This restatement is a proposal. Owner resolution O-1: V0 to V3 are descriptive planning labels, not implementation gates, until the Owner separately approves the proposed scale. The accepted ADR 0033 D13 rule still applies: when a Pekko oracle exists, V3 requires a differential scenario; when no applicable oracle exists, alternative evidence must be documented and explicitly approved by the Owner, and such rows remain `pending approval` until then. Existing repository gates and each story's accepted criteria still apply. Inventory rows record the evidence kinds (public-API test, ported spec, Go-side scenario, differential scenario, alternative evidence, approval reference) next to the descriptive label.

