### 5.3 Typed supervision contracts (inputs for A-02; from `SupervisionSpec` and `internal/Supervision.scala`)

Default Stop with `PostStop` (l.387, 502); restart sends `PreRestart` only, resets state (l.512), returned behavior ignored; `withLimit` window from the first failure, expired window resets to 1 (`updateRestartCount`); backoff delay and `resetBackoffAfter`; restart stashes messages and signals (`StashBuffer[Any]`, default `restart-stash-capacity=1000`), overflow publishes `Dropped(msg, "Stash is full in [RestartSupervisor]", self)`; restart with start failure: unlimited retries rethrows, limited rethrows only when `(restartCount+1) >= maxRestarts` and the deadline has time left (`Supervision.scala:300-302`); `stopChildren=true` replaces `watchWith` by `watch`; `ScheduledRestart(owner)` is ignored by non-owner supervisors; supervision wraps the adapter function (l.1575); `DeathPactException` supervisable (l.1408); strategy matrix at l.1659-1695. `Supervisor.apply` rejects an `AbstractBehavior` outside `setup`.

## 6. Hazards for implementers

- `kit-logger` mock: drops `With` arguments, `SetLevel` no-op, `Entries` unsynchronized; real `Sampling`/`RateLimit` can silently drop entries. `Config.Logger` is nil-silent. `With` per actor allocates a logger: not per message.
- `golang.org/x/time` in `pekko-actor/go.mod` is indirect via kit-logger; do not use it in actor code.
- CI test filter skips tests whose file or function names match `(integration|architecture|guard|judge|benchmark|testdata|fixture|e2e|system_test|timing|stress|subprocess|realprocess|allocation_contract)` or that use `time.Sleep`, `time.After`, `testing.Short` (`ci-fast.go:36,116-120`). Timer tests must use the manual clock and avoid these names, or they silently stop running in CI.
- gocyclo counts per function literal; split large interpreters.
- Stash replay: upstream drains in one turn ahead of new messages; Go has no head insert (NEW-08).
- `DeadLetter` shape: upstream asserts `DeadLetter(msg, sender, recipient)`; Go has `{Msg, To}`; sender assertions use ADR 0032 D3, D4 and D6 (accepted) with an explicit sender; ADR 0032 D5 does not apply to them.

